foundation.question_text:
The graph shows the monthly share price of Company A over a 6-month period.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[gray!30,very thin,xstep=1,ystep=1] (0,0) grid (6,5);
\draw[->,thick] (0,0) -- (6.5,0) node[below right,font=\small] {Month};
\draw[->,thick] (0,0) -- (0,5.5) node[above left,font=\small] {Price (\$)};
\foreach \x/\m in {1/Jan,2/Feb,3/Mar,4/Apr,5/May,6/Jun} \node[below,font=\small] at (\x,0) {\m};
\foreach \y/\v in {1/4.00,2/4.50,3/5.00,4/5.50,5/6.00} \node[left,font=\small] at (0,\y) {\v};
\node[below left,font=\small] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[very thick,blue] (1,1.4) -- (2,2.6) -- (3,2.0) -- (4,3.2) -- (5,4.2) -- (6,3.6);
\foreach \pt in {(1,1.4),(2,2.6),(3,2.0),(4,3.2),(5,4.2),(6,3.6)} \fill[blue] \pt circle (2.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What was the share price at the beginning of May?

The graph shows the share price of an energy company from July to December.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[gray!30,very thin,xstep=1,ystep=1] (0,0) grid (6,5);
\draw[->,thick] (0,0) -- (6.5,0) node[below right,font=\small] {Month};
\draw[->,thick] (0,0) -- (0,5.5) node[above left,font=\small] {Price (\$)};
\foreach \x/\m in {1/Jul,2/Aug,3/Sep,4/Oct,5/Nov,6/Dec} \node[below,font=\small] at (\x,0) {\m};
\foreach \y/\v in {1/11.00,2/12.00,3/13.00,4/14.00,5/15.00} \node[left,font=\small] at (0,\y) {\v};
\node[below left,font=\small] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[very thick,blue] (1,2.5) -- (2,1.8) -- (3,3.2) -- (4,4.0) -- (5,3.5) -- (6,4.8);
\foreach \pt in {(1,2.5),(2,1.8),(3,3.2),(4,4.0),(5,3.5),(6,4.8)} \fill[blue] \pt circle (2.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What was the share price at the start of September?

The graph tracks a tech company's share price over 8 months.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[gray!30,very thin,xstep=1,ystep=1] (0,0) grid (8,5);
\draw[->,thick] (0,0) -- (8.5,0) node[below right,font=\small] {Month};
